A||N||5||2xsess||Manual Mirror to Power Switch, need advice||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||10-03-2000||09:19 PM||||I'm thinking of stripping the power mirror setup off an 86GT. I searched the archives and didn't find any threads. <P>Any tips or help would be greatly appreciated. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||10-03-2000||09:24 PM||||Adding power mirrors is pretty simple. Remove the manual mirror shrouds, install powre mirrors. Will have to remove inner door panels, but isn't very difficult. I removed the dash so I could run wiring in stock location, but isn't required. Other than that, there is a solid orange wire(I think, don't remember too well) that plugs into the fuse box. Splice into it for the mirror power power line(this wire is hot all the time). Pretty simple and straight forward. Just about anyone can acomplish it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||10-04-2000||01:48 PM||||Power mirrors have their own wiring harness that is independent of the locks/windows wiring. There is a ground lug on the passenger side where the courtesy light is. When you pull the old wiring out you will seel how much has to be pulled to install it. The doner's dashboard will have to com out but not the recipiant, yo can just tuck them up under the dash and tie=wrap them to something to keep them from dropping down. The center console must be removed and the radioheater bezels/surround to run the switch wires so yo will have plenty of room to work. The plastic carpet trim covers the holes that the wires will come in from the doors. Be sure that the wires from the mirrors are tucked away from any movement of the windows. The factory install had them attached to a vertical support with a plastic stud. The only problem I have had is finding a drivers door panel without the joystick thingy. Right now I have the old one still there with the cables hacked off inside the door. I put my mirrors on when I did my dew strips since the mirrors hold them on as well. P/M is a worthwhile mod if taller and shorter drivers are using the car and fun to play with too!<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-04-2000||03:49 PM||||Many moons ago there was a thread discussing alternate uses for the manual mirror joystick bezel.  One creative use was to install a pushbutton switch to disarm the headlight motors so they could be left open with the lights off.<P>Another use was for mounting a security alarm  indicator LED.<P>How about a Fog Light switch or a machine gun trigger for heavy traffic situations?<P>You get the picture.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
